      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "While account-level metrics identify which companies are active, individual-level engagement reveals who within that account is engaged and with what content. This distinction is crucial because buying decisions in B2B involve multiple stakeholders. Understanding the specific behaviors of a VP of Marketing versus an IT manager, for example, allows for tailored messaging and content. Folloze champions this approach, asserting that account selection tells you where to focus, but individual-level engagement tells you what to do next, driving deeper engagement across buying groups."
