      "name": "What types of account engagement signals should B2B marketers track?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Marketers should track a mix of first- and third-party signals. Key categories include website engagement (pages visited, time spent), content consumption depth (whitepaper downloads, webinar attendance), email interaction patterns (opens, clicks, replies), third-party intent data (research on external sites), digital ad and social engagement, and crucial buying group breadth and depth (number and seniority of engaged individuals). Each signal provides context to the buyer's journey."
      }
